  fx.1 reveal f_letter
  fx.2 set flag:letter_told
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1228.VQ_PAST_SCHOOL.d
  t.any.1 College plan's unfinished.. ask about something I actually finished
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1228.VQ_PAST_SCHOOL.d2
  t.any.1 Don't read the folded letter or ask Mom about it
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1228.VQ_PAST_SCHOOL.d3
  t.any.1 The letter stays in my pocket.. stop trying to make me unfold it
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1228.VQ_PAST_TROUBLE
  t.lo.1 Accused of taking rent money.. didn't take it
  t.mid.1 Mavis found the cash with another lodger.. apology didn't get said as loudly as the accusation
  t.hi.1 Wanted being right about that to settle everything.. being right about one thing didn't settle the room
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1228.VQ_PAST_WORK
  t.lo.1 Looking for work in Louisville.. no steady job to put a neat label on
  t.mid.1 Wanted a room of my own before looking.. found out those plans don't line up politely
  t.hi.1 Could count a day's money fine on paper.. paper didn't need bus fare to get to work
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1228.VQ_TALK_AGE
  t.any.1 Eighteen.. birthday already happened, no family vote needed
  t.any.2 Eighteen since spring.. Mom still says it like she's checking the sum
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1228.VQ_TALK_DISLIKES
  t.any.1 People borrowing the scorecard pencil and keeping it till the inning's over
  t.any.2 Being told Mom already answered.. wasn't her question
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1228.VQ_TALK_FEAR
  t.lo.1 Quiet so complete I start thinking the radio's broken
  t.mid.1 Used to hear Grandma's two rings from outside.. now a silent house keeps me listening
  t.hi.1 When everything stops I count the little noises.. your chair moving helps more than being told it's fine
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1228.VQ_TALK_FOOD
  t.lo.1 Whatever doesn't come with a lecture about eating it
  t.mid.1 Grandma's potatoes.. she always claimed somebody else wanted the brown bits
  t.hi.1 Would like a ballpark supper again.. greasy paper and Ellen disputing the score
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1228.VQ_TALK_FROM
  t.any.1 Vine Grove originally.. had a room in Louisville for a while
  t.any.2 Grandma's place near Vine Grove was the easy address.. Louisville needed explaining
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1228.VQ_TALK_HABIT
  t.any.1 Tap the scorecard pencil twice before writing.. Ellen said the score won't change for waiting
  t.any.2 Amen.. there, did it again, wasn't asking you to pray
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1228.VQ_TALK_HOPE
  t.lo.1 An answer from a doctor that isn't Mom deciding for me
  t.mid.1 Keep thinking a Guard truck has a destination written somewhere.. would like one readable plan
  t.hi.1 Room with a table big enough for records.. haven't given up wanting stupid ordinary furniture
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1228.VQ_TALK_HOWARE
  t.lo.1 Fine if the next question isn't how far I can walk
  t.mid.1 Made it to the mat without Mom narrating.. count that as a foul if she starts now
  t.mid.2 Fine. You can believe the word without believing all the confidence
  t.mid.3 I don't need checking on every time I stop talking
  t.mid.4 Better being asked than hearing Mom answer for me
  t.hi.1 Don't need a brave answer from me?.. would like a chair more than I'd like to perform one
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1228.VQ_TALK_LIKES
  t.any.1 A score you can check.. no one gets to say the third inning happened differently
  t.any.2 Record sleeves with somebody's old price still penciled on.. makes me want to ask where they found it
  t.any.3 Baseball talk that stays baseball talk. No lesson hidden in the score
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1228.VQ_TALK_LUCK
  t.any.1 Baseball has enough bad bounces without calling my whole day luck
  t.any.2 Finding Mom was luck.. doesn't settle every argument we had before it
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1228.VQ_TALK_MUSIC
  t.any.1 Old records.. bought used ones because choosing mattered more than having the latest
  t.any.2 Mom remembers every song as too loud.. Grandma asked what the singer was saying
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1228.VQ_TALK_NAME
  t.any.1 Connie Webb.. you can ask me, Mom doesn't have to introduce the whole history
  t.any.2 Connie.. Ellen calls me umpire when she wants a pencil borrowed
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1228.VQ_TALK_NERVOUS
  t.lo.1 Keep checking the room key.. doesn't mean I need you to take it away
  t.mid.1 Talk too quickly when a stranger asks where I've been.. can hear it now
  t.hi.1 If I give you three answers pick the corrected one.. Ellen learned to wait for it
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1228.VQ_TALK_PRAYER
  t.any.1 Say amen when Mom's listing instructions.. she doesn't always notice which speech I'm ending
  t.any.2 Grandma prayed quietly.. preferred that to being asked afterward what I'd learned
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1228.VQ_TALK_QUIET
  t.any.1 Keep a little sound going please.. don't need a conversation, just somebody moving a cup
  t.any.2 May sit without telling you the entire notebook?.. quiet's better when I chose it
  t.any.3 Yeah. We can have a pause without calling it a problem
  t.any.4 Don't go on my account. I can like having you here and not have a story ready
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1228.VQ_TALK_SLEEP
  t.any.1 A little.. don't need Mom to announce when I shut my eyes
  t.any.2 Notebook makes a terrible pillow.. already checked that possibility
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1228.VQ_TALK_SPORTS
  t.lo.1 Baseball.. actual scores, not arguing which team deserves better luck
  t.mid.1 Ellen called an error on a clean catch once.. scorecard nearly ended our afternoon
  t.hi.1 Could show you the old scores.. promise not to pretend you're interested if you're not
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1228.VQ_TALK_STORY
  t.mid.1 Ellen borrowed my pencil for one score.. then kept asking to correct another, so I watched a whole inning without writing anything and blamed her for missing the best play
  t.hi.1 Ellen took my pencil at a ballgame.. spent the best play watching it instead of the field.. she described everything I'd missed.. count that as a foul on me
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1228.VQ_TALK_WEATHER
  t.any.1 Dry weather for the scorecard.. that's all the forecast I can personally use
  t.any.2 Cloudy would do.. sun makes every piece of road look longer than it is
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1228.VQ_WORLD_GUARD
  t.any.1 Haven't met a Guardsman I could ask.. trucks should have somebody deciding where they go, want to find that person
  t.any.2 Haven't seen a truck taking passengers.. saying I want one isn't news that one exists
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1228.VQ_WORLD_HOSPITAL
  t.lo.1 Don't know a working hospital.. need a doctor, have you actually seen one anywhere?
  t.mid.1 No hospital I've checked myself.. Mom's a nurse, still need someone who hears my answer without remembering every other answer I gave
  t.hi.1 Can't name an open hospital.. would take an examination without a neat promise, can't walk on somebody's confidence
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1228.VQ_WORLD_LAW
  t.any.1 Haven't seen a sheriff on our stretch.. want rules that mean the same thing whichever adult asks
  t.any.2 No news of anybody enforcing laws here.. keep thinking how Mavis had to admit she was wrong about the cash, wish there were still someone making that happen
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1228.VQ_WORLD_NEWS
  t.any.1 Heard a driver say the Guard had trucks farther on.. wrote driver said in the notebook, not confirmed
  t.any.2 Somebody said the Guard still had trucks.. somebody isn't much of a source, I know
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

