  t.any.2 Bought a boot lace and still let Brent use his spare.. new one vanished in the room
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1250.VQ_PAST_PROUD
  t.any.1 Got onto a line crew after helper work.. nobody carried me there
  t.any.2 One batch of peaches came out as good as Mavis's.. she checked the whole shelf before admitting it
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1250.VQ_PAST_REGRET
  gate.rule trust>=70 & alone & flag:receipt_told
  t.any.1 Father didn't trip in ninety-two.. confronted me over the canner sale.. shoved him into the porch rail, hurt his hip.. let Mavis believe he'd tripped.. that's the bit I keep stopping before I tell her
  cb.1 Leonard's hip was my doing.. wasn't a loose board or his bad footing
  fx.1 reveal f_father
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1250.VQ_PAST_REGRET.d
  t.any.1 What happened with father.. not telling it in company
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1250.VQ_PAST_REGRET.d2
  t.any.1 More than the sale.. want to say it once without a crowd
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1250.VQ_PAST_SCHOOL
  t.any.1 Finished in eighty-six.. went to Otis after that
  t.any.2 Brandenburg school.. could do sums better when there wasn't a clock ticking over me
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1250.VQ_PAST_WORK
  t.lo.1 Line crew.. helper before that
  t.mid.1 Started carrying an electrician's things in eighty-six.. line work from eighty-nine
  t.hi.1 Line crew.. liked being useful up there more than being clever down here
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1250.VQ_TALK_AGE
  t.any.1 Twenty-five.. sixty-eight baby
  t.any.2 Twenty-five.. old enough to have bought better boots twice
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1250.VQ_TALK_DISLIKES
  t.any.1 A good boot with one eyelet bent.. ruins the whole morning
  t.any.2 Brent asking how many miles the motorcycle did.. he knows damn well
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1250.VQ_TALK_FEAR
  t.any.1 Church bells.. sudden loud one gets me moving before I think
  t.any.2 A bell starting overhead.. don't laugh till you've seen how fast I duck
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1250.VQ_TALK_FOOD
  t.any.1 Beans and cornbread.. know that's not a grand answer
  t.any.2 Mavis's canned peaches.. cold enough the jar sweats
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1250.VQ_TALK_FROM
  t.any.1 Brandenburg.. room near my cousins' fence
  t.any.2 Brandenburg.. could reach next door without getting through breakfast
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1250.VQ_TALK_HABIT
  t.any.1 Whistle's in my hand.. little train stays quiet indoors
  t.any.2 Picking the boot lace knot.. Brent tied it better than I can undo it
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1250.VQ_TALK_HOPE
  t.any.1 Mavis letting me finish a sentence before she shuts the door
  t.any.2 Cousins still arguing over who borrowed the shovel.. means they're both there
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1250.VQ_TALK_HOWARE
  t.lo.1 Still got both boots.. one good lace between them
  t.lo.2 Kevin.. mostly dirt, some useful parts
  t.mid.1 Could sleep.. jokes start repeating if I don't
  t.mid.2 Feet hurt.. motorcycle would've hurt my wallet instead
  t.mid.3 Could make a joke. Wouldn't be answering, though
  t.mid.4 I keep saying fine faster than I can check whether I mean it
  t.mid.5 Better for having somebody let me change the first answer
  t.hi.1 Want Mavis to answer when I knock.. don't know if she will
  t.hi.2 Not asking you to make a good fellow out of me
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1250.VQ_TALK_JOKE
  t.any.1 Brent said my motorcycle saved fuel.. hard to burn any with the engine on his table
  t.any.2 Mavis labelled one jar Kevin's mistakes.. empty jar, said she hadn't bought one big enough
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1250.VQ_TALK_LIKES
  t.any.1 Canning beans with Mavis.. clean jar mouths, hot kitchen
  t.any.2 Making Dee's little ones laugh.. little train whistle does most of the work
  t.any.3 Getting a jar to seal on the first try. Still count that as a good afternoon
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1250.VQ_TALK_MUSIC
  t.any.1 Fast songs in the crew truck.. kept us from hearing each other complain
  t.any.2 Radio with a decent fiddle.. Brent changes it just to watch me argue
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1250.VQ_TALK_NAME
  t.any.1 Kevin Farley.. the line crew had less polite names
  t.any.2 Farley.. Kevin, not one of the cousins
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1250.VQ_TALK_NERVOUS
  t.any.1 Some.. mouth tries to outrun it
  t.any.2 Yes.. Mavis comes to mind when the jokes run out
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1250.VQ_TALK_QUIET
  t.any.1 Fine by me.. whistle won't object
  t.any.2 Good.. mouth could use a rest before it costs me something else
  t.any.3 Yes. Let's see if I can leave a silence alone for once
  t.any.4 You can stay. I haven't got a joke that improves on the company
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1250.VQ_TALK_SLEEP
  t.any.1 Sleep fine once I quit trying to be funny
  t.any.2 Could do with longer.. boots keep waking me where the heels rub
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1250.VQ_TALK_STORY
  t.any.1 Dee's boy thought my whistle ran a real train.. blew it from the porch every morning.. third day he asked why the train was so late.. told him it had my motorcycle engine.. Dee didn't let me escape that one
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1250.VQ_TALK_WEATHER
  t.any.1 Wouldn't mind rain after these cuffs are dry.. so probably in December
  t.any.2 Clouds might give us something.. don't trust my weather guesses over your eyes
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1250.VQ_WORLD_HOPE
  t.any.1 Things come round.. hope the good ones do too
  t.any.2 Yes.. still got people worth going home to, if they're there
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1250.VQ_WORLD_KIDS
  t.any.1 Dee had her two at home last I knew.. no newer word
  t.any.2 Would give children the first food.. small stomach doesn't mean small need
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1250.VQ_WORLD_NEWS
  t.any.1 Line crew stopped where we were.. nobody gave me a reason I could check
  t.any.2 Heard people naming shelters.. haven't met one who'd come out of those places
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1250.VQ_WORLD_POWER
  t.any.1 Can't promise how long.. line crew's not the whole supply
  t.any.2 Some lights were on when I left the truck.. that isn't a promise for here
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1250.VQ_WORLD_ROAD
  t.any.1 Got past on foot.. couldn't tell you a clear truck route
  t.any.2 A few miles looked passable.. maybe fewer, boots make miles feel ambitious
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1250.leave.angry
  t.any.1 Going.. jokes are staying in my mouth this time
  t.any.2 Had my fill of here.. boots can put up with another walk
  tag.1 kind:leave
end

node vp_1250.leave.plain
  t.any.1 Boot lace checked.. ready enough
  t.any.2 Kevin Farley.. if Mavis asks, tell her I'm trying home
  tag.1 kind:leave
end

node vp_1250.react.gave_book
  gate.rule gave:book
  t.any.1 Will see what it says once these cuffs are clean
  t.any.2 Thank you.. Dee would say read it before claiming I knew it already
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1250.react.gave_food
  gate.rule gave:food
  t.any.1 Thanks.. can't talk my way out of being grateful for food
  t.any.2 That helps.. Mavis would ask if I said thank you properly
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1250.react.gave_water
  gate.rule gave:water
  t.any.1 Appreciate the water.. whistle stays dry in my pocket
  t.any.2 Thank you.. was doing more talking than asking for what I needed
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1250.react.insult
  t.any.1 Funny stopped being funny there
  t.any.2 Heard it.. don't need you polishing the insult for me
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1250.react.refused
  t.any.1 All right.. won't try joking you into it
  t.any.2 Fair enough.. will stop working my mouth at it
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1250.react.threat
  t.any.1 Whoa.. whistle's staying put
  t.any.2 Don't.. can be quiet without getting hurt over it
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1250.return.arrive
  gate.rule visits>=1
  t.any.1 Farley back.. whistle still in the pocket
  t.any.2 Kevin again.. remembered your place without Brent correcting the turn
  tag.1 kind:return
end

node vp_1250.return.gave_food
  gate.rule visits>=1 & gaveever:food
  t.any.1 Remember the food you shared.. made the walk easier to face
  t.any.2 Your help with food mattered.. wouldn't want to return acting like it didn't
  tag.1 kind:return
end
